{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-7169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position $x$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $x(t)={t}^{2}(2t+4).$ Calculate the velocity at time $t=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-7169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[{t}^{2}(2t+4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}+8t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =6(2)^{2}+8(2) \\\\  & =24+16 \\\\  & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-7169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1b07b31af822a8036c908f3cca20c95455aea4a8db744d93c4827b74b3bdb67f"} {"question" "q-7169" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-7169" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "v=14"] ["math" "v=22"] ["math" "v=32"] ["math" "v=38"] ["math" "v=40"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-7169" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "v=40"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-7175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in centimeters) at time $t$ seconds is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=\\frac{5t-10}{t},\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-7175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{5t-10}{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=2,$ the velocity is\n\n$$\nv(2)=\\frac{10}{(2)^{2}}=\\frac{10}{4}=2.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|2.5|=2.5\\,\\text{cm/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-7175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1b07b31af822a8036c908f3cca20c95455aea4a8db744d93c4827b74b3bdb67f"} {"question" "q-7175" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-7175" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1.5\\,\\text{cm/s}"] ["math" "2.0\\,\\text{cm/s}"] ["math" "2.5\\,\\text{cm/s}"] ["math" "3.0\\,\\text{cm/s}"] ["math" "4.0\\,\\text{cm/s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-7175" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2.5\\,\\text{cm/s}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-336138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position $x$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\nx(t)=16\\sqrt{t}-{t}^{4},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity at time $t=1.$\n\n$v(1)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-336138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The velocity is the derivative of the position function $x(t)$ with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(16\\sqrt{t}-{t}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{2\\sqrt{t}}-4{t}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}-4{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1}}-4({1}^{3}) \\\\  & =8-4 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-336138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1b07b31af822a8036c908f3cca20c95455aea4a8db744d93c4827b74b3bdb67f"} {"question" "q-336138" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-336138" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-336166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement $s$ (in meters) relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by the equation $s(t)=\\frac{{2}^{t}}{{2}^{t}+1}$, where $t$ is the time, measured in seconds. Find the position ${s}_{0}$ and velocity ${v}_{0}$ of the particle at the initial moment of time $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n${s}_{0}=$\n{{field-1}}$\\text{m}\\,\\text{and}\\,$\n\n${v}_{0}=$\n{{field-2}}$\\text{m/s}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-336166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To calculate the initial position, we substitute $t=0$ it into the equation $s(t)=\\frac{{2}^{t}}{{2}^{t}+1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{0} & =s(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{0}}{{2}^{0}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{2}^{t}}{{2}^{t}+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{({2}^{t}+1)\\cdot {2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-{2}^{t}\\cdot {2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{({2}^{t}+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{({2}^{t}+1)}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=0\\,\\text{s},$ we substitute $t=0$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{0} & =v(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{0}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{({2}^{0}+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4}\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-336166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1b07b31af822a8036c908f3cca20c95455aea4a8db744d93c4827b74b3bdb67f"} {"question" "q-336166" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-336166" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-336166" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-336166" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\ln(2)}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-336186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in inches) at time $t$ minutes is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=3{t}^{4}-4{e}^{t},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=0\\,\\text{min}.$\n\nThe speed of the particle is \n{{field-1}}$\\text{in/min}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-336186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{4}-4{e}^{t}) \\\\  & =12{t}^{3}-4{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=0,$ the velocity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(0) & =12\\cdot {0}^{3}-4{e}^{0} \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-4|=4\\,\\text{in/min}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-336186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1b07b31af822a8036c908f3cca20c95455aea4a8db744d93c4827b74b3bdb67f"} {"question" "q-336186" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"} {"question" "q-336186" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13971693/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddfe4a87b0f68c795fddc39cae5357b6f64ff15eecad843f5f3325c293deca39"}] "usage" {"q-7175" []} "basis" 782 "retractions" [[17592186064856 :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nThe position $s(t)$ of a particle (in centimeters) at time $t$ seconds is given by\n$s(t) = \\frac{5t - 10}{t}, t > 0$.\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t = 2s$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186063647 17592186063648 17592186063649 17592186063650 17592186063651] "immutable_fields" [[17592186063646 :answer-field/correct] [17592186063646 :answer-field/id] [17592186063646 :answer-field/key] [17592186063646 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
